<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <!--
      Orbin's mark: an orbit, and the one body on it. Two shapes, one colour.

      It lives here rather than in either application module because both apps wear it, and it was
      previously copied into each of them — two files that could drift, describing themselves in
      comments as being the same.

      The ring breaks where the body sits rather than passing behind it. That is what keeps the
      shape legible at 36px, where a ring with a dot merely resting on it reads as a ring with a
      lump; this was checked by rendering it at every launcher size and mask, not assumed.

      The colour is `next.accent` from the dark palette. The interface is warm ink on warm paper
      with a single terracotta accent, and the mark this replaced was still drawn in the blue and
      purple of a palette the app no longer uses anywhere.

      Everything stays within a radius of 29 from centre; the adaptive-icon safe zone is 33.
    -->
    <path
        android:strokeColor="#F08A5A"
        android:strokeWidth="8"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:fillColor="#00000000"
        android:pathData="M74.92,47.2 A22,22 0 1 1 53.23,32.01" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="#F08A5A"
        android:pathData="M66.62,35.98 m-7,0 a7,7 0 1,0 14,0 a7,7 0 1,0 -14,0" />
</vector>
